# Imagery working tree.
#
# The rule: track what DEFINES an image, ignore what merely RECORDS one run.
#
# Tracked, deliberately:
#   jobs.json        the prompt set + styleHash — the contract that says which
#                    food each filename is. Without it a downloaded file is
#                    an anonymous jpeg.
#   reuse-map.json   which dravyas reuse an existing archive frame instead of
#                    generating. build_food_index.py reads it.
#   results/ledger.json
#                    which Flow mediaId produced which food. This is what makes
#                    a failed download recoverable without regenerating, so it
#                    is the one run artifact worth keeping forever.
#   the scripts.

# --- run logs: one machine, one sitting, no value to anyone else -------------
*.log
loop-state.txt

# --- per-run scratch. The leading underscore is the convention. --------------
results/_*

# --- working directories the scripts create and consume locally --------------
# accepted/ holds absolute paths from the machine that validated the images,
# so it is meaningless in anyone else's checkout even though the archive build
# reads it.
accepted/
queue/
done/
failed/
__pycache__/

# --- build output: archive 2 lands here, and the mp4s must never be committed
dist/
